# Publish new build

When the user says **Publish new build** (any capitalization), do this **in order**. Do not build the installer until GitHub has the new version and docs.

1. **Version** — bump `__version__` in `src/inventory_parser/__init__.py` (patch unless the user asked otherwise).
2. **Changelog** — move `## [Unreleased]` notes into `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` (today's date). Leave an empty Unreleased section.
3. **Docs** — update README.md, `wiki/*.md` (the how-to), `docs/index.html`, and Discord instruction files so they match this release. Leave `HowToUse.md` as a stub that points at the wiki; do not put a second full guide there. Do not invent Defender/zip “fixes”. Do not commit `docs/img/EQGM_icon.png`.
4. **Tests** — `py -3 -m pip install -e .` then `py -3 -m pytest -q` from the repo root. Fix failures before publishing.
5. **Push source** — commit the version and docs, `git push origin main`. If wiki pages changed, copy `wiki/*.md` to a clone of `EQ-Gear-Management.wiki.git` and push that too (use `GIT_AUTHOR_NAME` / `GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL` env for that clone; do not run `git config`).
6. **Installer last** — only after origin has the commit, run `publish_release.bat` (needs `gh auth login`, Nuitka, and Inno Setup 6). That builds locally and creates the GitHub Release with `EQGM-install-x.y.z.exe`. Do not `git add` `dist/`.

Pushing `main` must not build the installer on Actions. Do not use `git push` alone as a substitute for this sequence.
